00:30:07.370 --> 00:30:09.370
So I think that's the thing that I look at

00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:11.163
is from an emotional standpoint is,

00:30:12.570 --> 00:30:14.520
I don't wanna be paralyzed by anything.

00:30:15.770 --> 00:30:20.190
I want to know that I can overcome things

00:30:20.190 --> 00:30:22.100
as hard as they may be

00:30:23.770 --> 00:30:25.250
where there's something that has happened

00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:28.660
and your relationships, your marriage,

00:30:28.660 --> 00:30:31.870
family, things that may have happened

00:30:31.870 --> 00:30:35.193
like you just have to think
okay, I'm gonna get through it.

00:30:36.863 --> 00:30:38.467
I'm going to bounce back.

00:30:38.467 --> 00:30:43.040
And the pain is something
that navigate through.

00:30:43.040 --> 00:30:45.020
I often say a lot of people too

00:30:45.020 --> 00:30:49.073
like sometimes there's nothing
to do, but to go through it.

00:30:52.140 --> 00:30:53.907
- You know, Allan, that's so true.

00:30:53.907 --> 00:30:56.900
And yet we spend a lot of time

00:30:56.900 --> 00:30:58.450
trying to not go through things

00:31:00.468 --> 00:31:02.224
in the way that in fact,

00:31:02.224 --> 00:31:04.720
there are social sort of norms about that.

00:31:06.080 --> 00:31:08.603
And it's unfortunate because there is,

00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:12.580
socially and culturally,
we've had so much pain

00:31:12.580 --> 00:31:16.140
that has gone around losing
a son, losing both parents.

00:31:16.140 --> 00:31:18.180
I mean, if we just stop for a moment

00:31:19.440 --> 00:31:22.280
and think about what that is

00:31:22.280 --> 00:31:25.520
how is the person who is
feeling that experiencing

00:31:26.380 --> 00:31:28.210
we might start to connect with each other.

00:31:28.210 --> 00:31:32.970
We might go back to that
built in coping that we have

00:31:32.970 --> 00:31:34.980
which has to do with connection

00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:39.410
in a way that we start to
understand each other differently.

00:31:39.410 --> 00:31:41.333
- At least you made me
think of something too

00:31:41.333 --> 00:31:44.720
that I appreciate this,
that sometimes the pain

00:31:45.820 --> 00:31:47.700
we place the pain in the wrong,

00:31:47.700 --> 00:31:49.260
no I shouldn't say in the wrong place,

00:31:49.260 --> 00:31:51.480
but like when something happens to us

00:31:51.480 --> 00:31:54.535
let's us say, a family
member, God forbid gets killed

00:31:54.535 --> 00:31:59.480
or a lot of our young
people, there's violence.

00:31:59.480 --> 00:32:02.130
And so we know that we're
gonna get through it

00:32:02.130 --> 00:32:07.130
but we keep all holding
on to why it happened.

00:32:07.380 --> 00:32:11.100
We hold on to the person
that made that decision

00:32:11.100 --> 00:32:14.190
to take a life or, and it's almost

00:32:14.190 --> 00:32:19.183
