00:42:32.300 --> 00:42:34.950
You believe in something
that's going to happen

00:42:34.950 --> 00:42:35.800
and hasn't happened yet.

00:42:35.800 --> 00:42:38.240
You don't see yet in front of you.

00:42:38.240 --> 00:42:42.940
And so I think that's what gives me hope.

00:42:42.940 --> 00:42:47.140
I think when I think about relationships

00:42:47.140 --> 00:42:52.140
they deep down people, they
want to have a connection,

00:42:52.310 --> 00:42:56.202
they wanna have a deeper
connection, understand themselves,

00:42:56.202 --> 00:42:58.810
but they haven't learned, they
haven't been in a situation

00:42:58.810 --> 00:43:02.510
in environment that's
allowed them to do it.

00:43:02.510 --> 00:43:04.915
So a lot of times we get
caught in why is this person

00:43:04.915 --> 00:43:08.600
on the main and nasty
and evil and all that?

00:43:08.600 --> 00:43:12.803
Well, you gotta think
about where their soil

00:43:12.803 --> 00:43:15.320
where their roots are,
where they've come from,

00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:17.220
what they've been through.

00:43:17.220 --> 00:43:18.930
And then you kind of think, okay

00:43:20.540 --> 00:43:22.100
I think that's the way I kind of try

00:43:22.100 --> 00:43:24.350
to look at people, look at life.

00:43:24.350 --> 00:43:27.160
So I try to see the good side,

00:43:27.160 --> 00:43:29.797
see how I can be the part of the solution

00:43:29.797 --> 00:43:31.973
and part of the other side of it.

00:43:33.050 --> 00:43:34.653
So like during this whole time,

00:43:35.690 --> 00:43:37.203
I kept thinking about vision.

00:43:38.100 --> 00:43:41.150
Like I kept thinking
about like use this time

00:43:41.150 --> 00:43:43.979
to really sharpen your vision.

00:43:43.979 --> 00:43:46.626
Since you can't go
anywhere, you can't do much

00:43:46.626 --> 00:43:49.503
use it to envision what
you wanna do when you can,

00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:52.240
and really train that side.

00:43:52.240 --> 00:43:53.590
And that part of and that's kind of

00:43:53.590 --> 00:43:56.210
where I still have been thinking about.

00:43:56.210 --> 00:44:00.200
So doing that when you start
thinking about what's possible

00:44:00.200 --> 00:44:02.160
what you can do, what you wanna do

00:44:03.040 --> 00:44:08.040
it helps a little bit more hope come in

00:44:08.040 --> 00:44:10.890
instead of looking at what's
going on now, what happened?

00:44:11.810 --> 00:44:13.660
You kind of look forward.

00:44:13.660 --> 00:44:17.280
So I think that's kind of something

00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:19.080
that I've tried to make intentional.

00:44:19.990 --> 00:44:23.140
- That's so good in so many
aspects of perspective too

00:44:23.140 --> 00:44:26.260
which I know we've talked about
in other situations before

00:44:26.260 --> 00:44:29.000
but just that perspective
on the big picture

00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:32.180
that God given perspective
that this isn't the end

00:44:32.180 --> 00:44:33.440
there's more in a common.

00:44:33.440 --> 00:44:35.080
Like you said, just
perspective on learning

00:44:35.080 --> 00:44:36.730
and where others are coming from to

00:44:36.730 --> 00:44:39.230
what they've gone through
and having that project.

00:44:42.370 --> 00:44:46.570
- I just believe too, like I
really believe that's a choice.

00:44:46.570 --> 00:44:48.760
A lot of people, you
guys know more than me

00:44:48.760 --> 00:44:50.810
like there are some imbalances

00:44:50.810 --> 00:44:54.190
and constructs that people have internally

00:44:54.190 --> 00:44:58.740
with their genetic makeup
and what's going on.

00:44:58.740 --> 00:45:00.860
But I do think that deep down

00:45:00.860 --> 00:45:03.770
we have to look at it at
our capacity as a choice.

00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:05.610
Like we have a choice
to look at it that way

00:45:05.610 --> 00:45:08.543
and believe that, and we
have to use that choice.

00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:14.600
- Yeah, I would add, I see
Allan's perspective fully

00:45:16.770 --> 00:45:19.380
of what he's saying is so important.

00:45:19.380 --> 00:45:24.380
I think the hope for me is
coming from the young people too.

00:45:25.870 --> 00:45:29.730
They are not happy,

00:45:29.730 --> 00:45:32.930
they are very up set
with what is going on.

00:45:32.930 --> 00:45:36.030
Just generally one had to
say, not everybody of course,

00:45:36.030 --> 00:45:39.420
but they have forced us to engage

00:45:39.420 --> 00:45:43.483
in a way that I had not seen before.

00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:49.340
And that it gives me hope
that they have basically

00:45:49.440 --> 00:45:51.200
whether it is school shootings

00:45:51.200 --> 00:45:54.650
whether it is shooting
violence that we're seeing,

00:45:54.650 --> 00:45:59.650
racial violence, whether
it's structural racism

00:46:02.455 --> 00:46:04.299
or microaggressions,

00:46:04.299 --> 00:46:08.940
or how COVID's response was,

00:46:08.940 --> 00:46:11.630
all of those pieces,
how it's affecting them,

00:46:11.630 --> 00:46:14.990
they're voicing their pain,
but they're also challenging us

00:46:14.990 --> 00:46:18.113
and at a very basic level,

00:46:19.160 --> 00:46:22.100
and they're expecting more.

00:46:22.100 --> 00:46:25.860
And so I think there's a hope in that

00:46:25.860 --> 00:46:30.070
because they've gone approaching life

00:46:30.070 --> 00:46:32.470
and approaching what's
happening in the world

00:46:32.470 --> 00:46:35.163
in a different way than
when we were younger.

00:46:36.160 --> 00:46:40.720
But also I think forcing
us to see their pain,

00:46:40.720 --> 00:46:45.170
which makes certainly motivates
me to say, this is not okay.

00:46:45.170 --> 00:46:46.670
We've got to do better.

00:46:46.670 --> 00:46:50.010
And it sort of appeals hopefully

00:46:50.010 --> 00:46:53.570
to our own better angels
to sort of come up

00:46:53.570 --> 00:46:56.100
with solutions to break
down barriers if we can,

00:46:56.100 --> 00:46:58.720
to sort of think outside the box,

00:46:58.720 --> 00:47:00.770
to not get stuck in the choices

00:47:00.770 --> 00:47:04.210
as Allan was saying to the sort
of think of alternate things

00:47:04.210 --> 00:47:05.420
and alternate choices

00:47:05.420 --> 00:47:10.420
and other alternate
perspectives, as you said Nii.

00:47:11.140 --> 00:47:14.141
And because it's amazing how that can be.

00:47:14.141 --> 00:47:16.070
There are lots of different ways

00:47:16.070 --> 00:47:18.183
you just have to open your mind up to it.

00:47:19.140 --> 00:47:23.510
And we are faced with a
really lots of challenges,

00:47:23.510 --> 00:47:26.554
but the hope is there.

00:47:26.554 --> 00:47:28.060
And we have to believe in it

00:47:28.060 --> 00:47:32.950
because we have to find a
better place in a better way.

00:47:32.950 --> 00:47:34.420
- Yeah, that's so true.

00:47:34.420 --> 00:47:36.200
And it ties together
what you're both saying,

00:47:36.200 --> 00:47:38.170
